q-values of Accept-Encoding (aZ, 22.11.2026): "zstd;q=0" was taken as an
acceptance, as "zstd" first in the header was without a look at what follows it.
Now as nginx takes "gzip" (ngx_http_gzip_ok, ngx_http_gzip_accept_encoding and
ngx_http_gzip_quantity of src/http/ngx_http_core_module.c of nginx 1.31.9, for
"zstd"): the common "zstd,..." first, else the first "zstd" that is a token
of its own, refused with q=0 (RFC 9110, 12.5.3), as HanadaLee f81c5f8 does.
Applied by post-patch in WRKSRC_zstd after extra-patch-zstd-window, -p0.

